In article <1992Oct13.060306.5901@nevada.edu>, funky@nevada.edu (MATTHEW KAPHAN) writes:
> What is the method to keep nymphs from stealing things from me, and 
> lepracauns also?  I just started playing the game, and I'm having a lot
> of trouble staying alive unless i'm in exploratory mode.  Any hints to help
> me out?

Spoilers!

The best method of avoiding problems with nymphs and leprechauns is not
to wake them (if the nymph appears at a fountain, bad luck).

Leprechauns are easy anyway, just drop all your gold before you enter the
room with the leprechaun.

A wand of cancellation will stop a nymph stealing from you. Failing
that, she will steal a ring of adornment first. If you have a mirror,
#apply it at the nymph and the nymph will steal the mirror rather than
anything else more important. They often seem to prefer your shield and
other rings, too, (this is just a personal observation, may or may not
be correct).  So if you can have a couple of encounters without having
the nymph steal anything important, you have a fair chance of killing
her. Throwing weapons are very handy for the purpose of weakening the
nymph.

A potion of speed makes it very easy.

If you find the nymph has stolen lots of your stuff, it may be an idea
to go back up a level or two and collect lots of junk, which lessens the
chance that your armour and good weapons will be lost in the next
encounter or two.

Unfortunately, sometimes you just have to accept the fact that the
little #@*?$! has stolen everything you have and you are about to die a
painful (naked) death.

  -dif-

